# Frontend Conventions

Data-driven single-page resume: Vue 3 `<script setup>`, Vite, strict TS, Tailwind v4, `@lucide/vue`.

## File naming

- Use **kebab-case** for every source file — components, composables, data, types, styles. Never PascalCase or camelCase filenames.
- The component's local name in imports/templates stays **PascalCase**; only the *filename* is kebab-case.
- Import components via the `src/components` barrel (`./components`), not deep paths — but intra-`components/` sibling imports stay direct to avoid cycles.

```text
✅ rich-text.vue   section-header.vue   resume-header.vue   use-theme.ts   themes.ts
❌ RichText.vue    SectionHeader.vue    useTheme.ts
```

```ts
// ✅ kebab-case file, PascalCase local name + usage
import RichText from './components/rich-text.vue' // <RichText :text="..." />
```

## Formatting (match `.prettierrc.json` / `.editorconfig` — do not deviate)

- 2-space indent, **no semicolons**, **single quotes**, no trailing commas, LF, final newline.
- Max line length 120. UTF-8. Trim trailing whitespace.

## TypeScript (strict)

- `strict`, `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters` are on — no dead vars/params, no implicit `any`.
- `verbatimModuleSyntax` is on: import types with `import type`, never a value import.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
import type { Profile } from '../types'
// ❌ BAD — breaks verbatimModuleSyntax
import { Profile } from '../types'
```

## Vue components

- Always `<script setup lang="ts">`. Block order: `<script>`, `<template>`, then `<style>` (only if needed).
- Props via generics. Use `withDefaults` only when defaults exist; capture `props` only when the script reads them.

```vue
<!-- ✅ template-only props -->
defineProps<{ label: string }>()
<!-- ✅ defaults needed -->
const props = withDefaults(defineProps<{ text: string; tag?: string }>(), { tag: 'span' })
<!-- ✅ derived state -->
const years = computed(() => new Date().getFullYear() - props.profile.experienceStartYear)
```

- Components are presentational and content-agnostic — they take typed props, never import `resume` data.

## Content / data

- All resume content lives in `src/data/resume.ts`, typed by `Resume` in `src/types.ts`. Edit data there, not in templates.
- Inline tech terms use backticks in data strings (e.g. `` '熟悉 `vue3` 开发' ``); `RichText.vue` renders `` `code` `` and `**bold**`. Don't hand-write `<code class="tech">` in markup.

## Styling — Tailwind v4

- Layout/spacing/color via utilities. Design tokens are CSS-first in `@theme` (`src/styles/main.css`): colors `paper` `paper-soft` `ink` `ink-soft` `ink-faint` `seal` `seal-deep` `line`; fonts `display` `sans` `mono`.
- Use token utilities (`text-ink`, `bg-paper/40`, `border-line`, `font-display`); never raw hex in markup.
- Named font-weight utilities (`font-semibold`), **not** `font-600`. Arbitrary values use brackets: `text-[13.5px]`, `max-w-[900px]`.
- Reach for scoped `<style>`/`main.css` only when utilities can't express it (e.g. masks/noise in `SealStamp.vue`, `.sheet`, `.tech`, keyframes).

## Icons (`@lucide/vue`)

- Import by name; size with numeric `:size`, color with text utilities. Brand icons (e.g. GitHub) don't exist — substitute (`Code` is used for GitHub).

```vue
import { Printer } from '@lucide/vue'
<Printer :size="15" class="text-seal" />
```

## Print / build

- `.no-print` for screen-only UI (toolbar); `.break-avoid` to keep blocks together across A4 pages. Print/`@page` rules live in `main.css`.
- Vite `base` is `/resume/`; build assets with `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`, not hardcoded paths.
